<title>FRANCE: PSA Peugeot 1996 net tumbles, div cut.</title>
<headline>PSA Peugeot 1996 net tumbles, div cut.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			     734  vs	   1,703</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)			  3  vs		 5</p>
<p>    Turnover				   172,668  vs	 164,248</p>
<p>NOTE - A compilation of broker forecasts by Paris consultant Jacques Cahine Finance showed a consensus expectation of 1.2 billion francs for net attributable profit and a wide range of individual estimates, from 800 million to 1.7 billion.  </p>
<p>    Operating				    1,675  vs	   3,751</p>
<p>    Gross result				 1,054  vs	   2,426</p>
<p>    Cashflow				    11,160  vs	  12,776</p>
<p>    Investments net			    9,894  vs	  10,044</p>
<p>    Net financial debt			 8,877  vs	   9,823</p>
<p>NOTE - The company released its results in a statement.</p>
<p>World vehicle sales in units were 2,006,100 versus 1,865,100 and world production in units was 1,979,000 versus 1,887,900.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
